4.4.1
---
- examples: the eleven qxapp classes that had a unit test but no visual sample now
  have one, as four family samples rather than one sample per class - a family is
  what a user looks at, and eleven windows over the same four ideas would have
  hidden that. Example_App_PropertyEditor covers QxProperty, QxPropertyEditor and
  QxSettingsDialog against one file-backed QxSettings, so an edit made in the form
  is the edit the dialog shows; Example_App_Buttons covers QxToolButton,
  QxMenuButton, QxMenuAccessButton and QxExtensionButton; Example_App_NavigationBar
  covers QxNavigationBar (the vertical rail, driving a page stack) and QxNavBar (a
  QxTabBar subclass with a customize menu) - different base classes behind similar
  names; Example_App_TabWidget covers QxTabWidget and QxTabBar. doc/pages/build.md
  example count 23 -> 27
- tests: one in-process smoke test per new sample. Each compiles the sample's own
  mainwindow.cpp, stands the window up offscreen and looks up the classes the sample
  exists for, so a sample cannot rot silently - if its source stops compiling or its
  window starts crashing, the test fails. Launching the sample executables through
  QProcess was tried first and does not work here: CreateProcess fails for them on
  Windows whatever the environment or working directory is, while the same
  executables start fine when launched by hand. The files live in
  tests/qxapp/examples/ because tests/qxapp/auto/ is swept by a tst_*.cpp glob that
  would have registered each of them a second time
- qxcore 0.1.2, qxtheme 0.1.1, qxwindow 0.3.1, qxribbon 0.12.1, qxdock 0.2.2,
  qxplugin 0.2.1, qxapp 0.1.1: unchanged. 4.4.1 touched examples, tests and docs
  only - src/libs has no change at all since the 4.4.0 tag - so no library version
  moves (K11)

4.4.0
---
- qxwindow 0.3.0 -> 0.3.1. Internal cleanup only - no public API changed, so the
  step is a patch. The frameless hit-test now asks the system buttons and the
  hit-test-visible items the same question from one place, and the private log
  macros are renamed QWK_* -> QXWINDOW_* with the category becoming "qxwindow"
  (was "qwindowkit"): set QT_LOGGING_RULES=qxwindow.*=true in place of
  qwindowkit.*. The window-context refactor is private to windowcontext_p.h and is
  unchanged in effect
- qxribbon 0.12.0 -> 0.12.1. Three bug fixes, none touching the exported surface,
  so a patch. RibbonCustomizeWidget recorded a "move down" on an action as a
  "move up" (the action branch handed -1 to makeChangeActionOrderCustomizeData,
  where -1 means up); the ribbon bar named its tab bar twice so the stacked widget
  was left unnamed; RibbonPage left two private fields uninitialised and a wheel
  event or scroll-button click before the first layout compared an indeterminate
  value. RibbonCustomizeWidget::isChanged() and model() are removed in this release
  - the class carries no export macro, so per the project red line ("not exported =>
  not API") that is not an API change and the version does not move on it
- qxdock 0.2.1 -> 0.2.2. Three bug fixes, patch. DockWindow left its globally locked
  features uninitialised, so every dock widget in a window reported a feature set
  with arbitrary bits removed; hideDockWidget() deleted the content of a
  DeleteContentOnClose widget that had been taken back on purpose and dereferenced a
  null pointer; pinning an already-pinned widget crashed because
  DockWidget::setAutoHide() / DockPanel::setAutoHide() only substituted a real side
  on the path that creates the auto-hide container, not on the path that moves an
  already-pinned widget (R7, R8, R12 in the 4.4 plan)
- qxcore 0.1.2, qxtheme 0.1.1, qxplugin 0.2.1, qxapp 0.1.1: unchanged. None of the
  four received a code change in 4.4 - every change in the tree was in tests,
  demos, or docs - so their versions stay where 4.3.0 left them. The version number
  is the library's statement of "did the interface move"; with no interface move it
  does not move (K11)
- tests: qxapp's seven leaf controls - QxTabBar, QxTabWidget, QxNavBar,
  QxToolButton, QxMenuButton, QxMenuAccessButton, QxExtensionButton - had no unit
  test at all and now have one each (tst_qxappwidgets), offscreen-only minimal
  assertions. The four property/settings classes were already covered. This is the
  curated half of the qxapp example gap; the visual samples land in 4.4.1
- demos: the qxwindow demo is back. It went away with the qmake-only demos and was
  rebuilt on the current API (setup() + setTitleBar(), the four system buttons with
  WindowIcon, the full set of window materials, showSystemMenu() on the icon button)
  rather than restored - the original leaned on a WindowStyleAgent and a
  WindowBar/WindowButton pair that were deleted in the same commit. It links qxwindow
  and nothing else
- docs: doc/pages/build.md lists the demo again and the example count is 23; the
  qxapp example modules that still lack a visual sample are noted for 4.4.1

4.3.0
---
- qxribbon 0.11.0 -> 0.12.0. FramelessHelper and the window class on top of it,
  RibbonWindow, are gone. Both were deprecated in 4.2 (K27 / K26) and the K26
  buffer - a removal waits at least one release - has now run out.
  FramelessHelper was the frameless backend qxribbon carried so that it needed no
  dependency on qxwindow; only its Windows + Qt 5 path was complete, and
  everywhere else a window first shown maximised could not be restored.
  RibbonWindow was RibbonMainWindow plus that backend and nothing else, so the
  two went together rather than leaving an empty shell behind. On every Qt
  version the answer is QxApp::RibbonAppWindow, which frames the same
  RibbonMainWindow through qxwindow's native path; on Qt 5 that costs a
  dependency on qxapp, and qxwindow's native backend does build there - checked
  before deleting, and the reason this did not wait for Qt 5 to be dropped.
  Every sample moves to RibbonMainWindow. RibbonGalleryViewport also loses its
  export macro: it lives in a private header, was privatized on purpose, and no
  caller names it. See doc/pages/migration.md, section "4.3 已删除"
- qxwindow 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0. WindowStyleAgent is gone (deprecated in 4.2 under
  K26), and so is the QX_WINDOW_CONFIG_STYLE_AGENT option that compiled it.
  HighContrast was the one value QxThemeManager does not report, and it had no
  consumer anywhere in the tree - checked before deleting, and the reason the
  class does not come back in a smaller "just HighContrast" form. The public
  surface is now two classes, and it was walked end to end: the only consumer in
  the tree is qxapp's RibbonAppWindow with six members, and the three members
  that had no test at all - centralize(), raise() and showSystemMenu() - have
  one now
- qxcore 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2, qxtheme 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1, qxdock 0.2.0 -> 0.2.1,
  qxplugin 0.2.0 -> 0.2.1, qxapp 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1. All five move by patch for the
  same one-line reason: QX_<LIB>_DEPRECATED_SINCE never answered true for a
  deprecation that had already happened, because
  QX_<LIB>_DISABLE_DEPRECATED_BEFORE defaulted to the library's own version and
  (0,11,0) > (0,11,0) is false. All seven libraries defined the macro and not
  one used it, so the mechanism was dead and a deprecation silently lasted
  forever. The default is now a fixed floor, and tst_qxdeprecated covers all
  seven libraries
- tests: qxdock had 8 exported classes that no test mentioned and qxribbon had
  12; both are covered now, 32 and 52 cases. Two bugs surfaced while writing
  them and are fixed: RibbonTheme::setTheme(RibbonTheme::CustomTheme)
  dereferenced the widget argument, whose documented default is a null pointer,
  and RibbonCtrlContainer built vertical centred its icon while one switched
  vertical afterwards left-aligned it
- qxwindow: the "frameless window cannot be maximised on first show" entry on
  the limitations page is no longer something only a person can notice. A probe
  reproduces it on a plain Qt window with no qtcanpool in it and is recorded as
  an expected failure on Qt 6 + Windows - measured as reproducing on 6.8.3 and
  passing on 5.15.2 - so the day the Qt plugin is fixed the case reports an
  unexpected pass instead of staying quiet. A second case guards the half the
  library controls: its own window must not ask Qt for a frameless window. That
  one holds offscreen and runs on every CI leg; the probe needs a window manager
  and skips there
- Qt 5: still supported and still built, and this release deletes none of it,
  but what a removal would mean is written down now. doc/pages/migration.md says
  who a removal in 5.0.0 affects - the library's own usage does not change,
  find_package and the QtCanpool:: targets are identical on Qt 6, while the
  caller's own Qt 5 usage does - what to do with the two qtcompat helpers, and
  that the thirty < 6.0 branches are mostly compile-time adaptations with a few
  that follow semantic changes in Qt itself. There is no date: K32 sets three
  trigger conditions instead
- docs: doc/pages/limitations.md records that CI does not cover Qt 6.12 (K31).
  That entry is deliberately marked as a boundary of the evidence rather than a
  known bad behaviour, and it says when it can be deleted; every "on Qt 6" claim
  on that page is evidence up to 6.8 only
- examples: the samples were checked against this release rather than changed to
  have something to show, because nothing in A1-A7 changed behaviour - A1
  removes a constant-false branch, A2 is an extraction, A3/A4/A6/A7 are tests
  and A5 is an assessment. One stale thing was found and fixed: a commented-out
  setRibbonTheme(RibbonTheme::WpsdarkTheme) in examples/qxribbon/simple named an
  enumerator that does not exist

4.2.0
---
- qxribbon 0.10.2 -> 0.11.0. FramelessHelper is deprecated (K27). It is the
  frameless backend of RibbonWindow and only really works on Windows with Qt 5;
  everywhere else - every Qt 6 platform included - it takes the incomplete half
  of the path, where a window first shown maximised cannot be restored. Use
  QxApp::RibbonAppWindow instead, which goes through qxwindow. Removal waits at
  least one more release under the K26 buffer; RibbonWindow itself is unchanged.
  RibbonStyleOption also gained setBaseHeight(), setTitleBarHeight() and
  setTabBarHeight(), so the ribbon size layout can be tuned without subclassing
- qxwindow 0.1.2 -> 0.2.0. WindowStyleAgent is deprecated (K26 / W2): nothing in
  the tree refers to it, no page documents it, it is not even compiled unless
  QX_WINDOW_CONFIG_STYLE_AGENT is on, and QxThemeManager in qxtheme already
  follows the system colour scheme more completely than this class does. The
  resize border geometry also moved out of windowcontext_qt.cpp into
  windowgeometry_p.h as plain functions over a QSize, so that arithmetic is
  covered by tests for the first time
- qxdock stays at 0.2.0. The 0.2.0 "perspective and group" surface - DockGroup,
  DockGroupManager and DockSubWindow - had neither a dedicated example nor any
  test until now; both were added (tst_DockGroup, examples/qxdock/dockgroup).
  Its single header change this cycle, dockautohidecontainer.h, is only the
  comment A13 added, which is not an API change under appendix B, so the number
  does not move; what changed is recorded in the library's own Unreleased
  section instead (K24)
- qxcore, qxtheme, qxplugin and qxapp do not move (0.1.1 / 0.1.0 / 0.2.0 /
  0.1.0): no public header of theirs changed at all this cycle. These four had
  no library-level changelog before; they do now (K24, non-retroactive)
- debt: every TODO and FIXME in src/libs and in the rest of the tracked tree is
  settled through one of K21's three exits - fixed with a regression test,
  rewritten as a NOTE pointing at an entry in doc/pages/limitations.md, or
  deleted with the reason written down
- examples: all 22 targets under examples/ now carry a one-line README, and
  Example_Dock_Group is new
- docs: doc/pages/release.md is new (K28) and holds every step of cutting a
  release in one page; the component dependencies and class names in index.md,
  architecture.md and components.md were corrected to match the code
- build and CI: projects/template is now rendered by scripts/new-project and
  compared byte for byte in CI; thirdparty/ and the redundant
  scripts/project.py are gone; the AUTOMOC workaround qtc_autogen_rescan() was
  re-verified on CMake 4.2.1 against both Qt 5 and Qt 6 and is still required
  (C3); the screenshot golden is now kept per Qt major version, because Qt 5 and
  Qt 6 do not produce the same window size and a shared golden made Qt 5 fail
  every time (C2)
- X11: qxdock's linux/ subtree does get compiled on the Ubuntu CI legs, but
  every test runs offscreen, so is_platform_x11() short-circuits each request:
  the xcb interaction layer has still never executed on CI (A15)

4.1.1
---
- qxribbon: make RibbonGridContainer's enter event an override again on Qt 6.
  Qt changed the parameter of that virtual from QEvent to QEnterEvent, so the
  Qt 5 signature did not override anything there - it hid the virtual, and the
  handler silently never ran, which left a ribbon menu with two entries looking
  current. The declaration is guarded by the Qt version now and both variants
  carry an override specifier, so the same mistake fails to compile instead.
  This is the one library change of the batch, and qxribbon follows it:
  0.10.1 -> 0.10.2
- qxdock: keep a widget auto hidden when it is added to a window that has
  nothing else open. The panel being filled was toggled open before it had ever
  been shown, and the dock widget read that as "this is pinned and there is
  nothing else open, so unpin it": the auto hide container was deleted on the
  spot, the widget came back as an ordinary docked one, and the panel created
  for the container was left behind in the root splitter. The leftover also put
  contentRect() on the splitter's never laid out default of 640x480 before the
  first layout, which the auto hide resize limit and the choice of side bar
  both read. Only the .cpp changed, so no library moved for it
- ci: generate the moc that qxpropertyeditor.cpp includes before clang-tidy
  looks at it, when that file is part of the change. The file defines its
  Q_OBJECT classes in the .cpp and includes its own .moc, so the analysis used
  to stop at that include and report nothing - which cannot be told apart from
  a clean run
- docs: add the seventh known limitation, the frameless window on Windows and
  Qt 6 that cannot be maximised on its first show, with a NOTE at the restore
  branch of framelesshelper.cpp pointing at it
- libs: only qxribbon moved (0.10.2) - ribboncontainers.h is the one public
  header this batch touched. The other six stand still, and the qxdock fix
  above lives in that library's Unreleased section because its interface did
  not change

4.1.0
---
- qxdock: scroll the active tab back into view. The code that did it sat
  commented out because the written form ended the process: a QTimer::singleShot
  callback captured the private pointer `q` by reference, so it read a stack slot
  that updateTabs() had already released. Rewritten to capture by value, guard
  the tab with a QPointer and coalesce the scrolls, with regression tests for
  both the behaviour and the crash
- qxribbon: start the frameless helper at the window's real DPI instead of a
  hardcoded 96. The pair of DPI slots is a "did the DPI change" flag, and
  starting both at 96 made the first real change look like no change at all -
  so the one moment that needs the frame repaired was the moment the flag
  suppressed it. Falls back from GetDpiForWindow to the desktop DC to 96
- build: take a source file added to the tree into account on the next build. A
  glob caches its result at configure time and AUTOMOC keeps its own list of
  what it has scanned, so neither noticed a new file - the add_qtc_* helpers now
  clear the autogen stamp at configure time and the globs use CONFIGURE_DEPENDS
- project: give the 16 TODO/FIXME notes in qxdock, qxribbon and qxapp a verdict
  each (2 fixed, 9 written up as limitations, 5 removed as questions that do not
  stand); the 8 inherited from Qt in qxwindow are not claimed
- docs: add doc/pages/limitations.md - six behaviours that are known and
  deliberate, each with its cause, why it stays, and what changing it would take
- ci: report clang-tidy findings on the lines a change touched rather than on
  every line of the files it touched, and put the coverage listing in the job
  summary; neither is a gate (K8), but a measurement worth taking has to be
  measured honestly first
- libs: no library moved this time - the public headers are untouched, and a
  version is a claim about an interface

4.0.0
---
- project: remove qmake for good; BREAKING: the 88 .pro / .pri files are gone,
  the four demos that only qmake still built are gone, and the examples that
  were qmake-only are rebuilt with CMake - building QtCanpool now means CMake
  and nothing else, see doc/pages/migration.md for what to change
- project: build the examples with CMake under WITH_EXAMPLES (on by default);
  22 of them recovered, with the target names they had under qmake
- qxplugin: new library holding the plugin contract (QxPlugin, QxPluginSpec),
  discovery and dependency resolution (QxPluginManager, Kahn ordering, cycles
  and missing dependencies reported as a named chain), the three-step lifecycle
  with failure isolation, the surface a plugin programs against
  (QxPluginContext) and the object pool that lets two plugins cooperate without
  either including the other's header (QxObjectPool)
- qxapp: add QxPluginManagerDialog - list, details, reverse dependencies and
  diagnostics, with the switches stored as deviations from the metadata so that
  the metadata stays the default
- qxapp: keep the shell out of the plugin contract; pluginContext() hands out a
  thin adapter, so the host's window class reaches no plugin, not even in a
  comment
- modules: add the src/modules sample layer (output, notebook, filetree) and an
  IDE-style demo assembled from them that names not one of them in its source
- project: normalize line endings to LF across the tree, with .gitattributes and
  a .git-blame-ignore-revs entry (see doc/ROADMAP-3.x.md, decision K20)
- test: cover the plugin runtime, the sample modules and the assembled demo
- docs: add the plugin guide, the 3.x -> 4.0 migration section, and the
  architecture and component pages for qxplugin
- libs: qxcore 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1, qxapp 0.0.1 -> 0.1.0, qxplugin starts at 0.2.0;
  qxtheme, qxwindow, qxribbon and qxdock did not move

3.3.0
---
- qxapp: add QxWorkspaceManager, which puts a name on what the shell already
  persisted - a workspace is the dock layout plus the current page, and never
  the window geometry, which belongs to the window
- qxapp: give QxAppShell the four workspace entry points a menu needs:
  workspaceManager(), workspaceNames(), saveWorkspace() and applyWorkspace()
- qxapp: give the status bar indicator a percentage mode; it is one widget with
  two modes now, busy and progress, and the last call wins
- demo: give named workspaces and the progress indicator a place in the ribbon
  of the AppShell demo
- test: cover the workspace manager and the progress indicator with unit tests
- docs: document named workspaces and the status bar progress

3.2.0
---
- project: remove the qcanpool library; BREAKING: the deprecated forwarding
  headers go with it, so the old QCanpool names no longer compile - 3.1 only
  warned, see doc/design/3.0-MIGRATION.md
- project: remove the qmake application template and the legacy qcanpool
  examples; qmake stays frozen, so nothing new was added to replace them
- qxcore: add QxTranslator to load, switch and enumerate translations
- qxapp: add QxToast and QxToastManager for in-application notifications
  (levels, timeout, hover to hold, stacking and eviction)
- qxapp: give QxAppShell its own toast stack plus a showToast() shortcut
- qxapp: add QxProperty and QxPropertyEditor, a key/value form generated from
  property descriptors
- qxapp: add QxSettingsDialog, a settings dialog that reads and writes a
  QxSettings object
- project: wire language switching, toasts and the settings dialog into
  projects/template and into scripts/new-project, so a generated application
  can do all three out of the box
- test: cover the translator, the toasts, the property editor and the settings
  dialog with unit tests
- docs: document i18n, toasts, the property editor kernel and the settings
  dialog
- docs: give the documentation home page a library version to project version
  table

3.1.0
---
- qcanpool: remove the legacy ribbon
  (ribbonbar/ribbonpage/ribbongroup/ribbonwindow/ribboncontainer); BREAKING: use qxribbon
  instead, see doc/design/3.0-MIGRATION.md
- qcanpool: drop the QCANPOOL_CONFIG_RIBBON build option
- qcanpool: remove the fancyribbon demo (superseded by the qxribbon demos)
- qcanpool: move the general-purpose legacy widgets to qxapp and rename them into the Qx
  namespace (FancyToolButton->QxToolButton, ExtensionButton->QxExtensionButton,
  MenuButton->QxMenuButton, MenuAccessButton->QxMenuAccessButton, TinyTabBar->QxTabBar,
  TinyTabWidget->QxTabWidget, TinyNavBar->QxNavBar); the old names stay as deprecated
  forwarding classes for one release
- qcanpool: remove the legacy window-chrome widgets; BREAKING: QuickAccessBar, FancyTitleBar,
  WindowLogo, WindowToolBar, MiniTabBar, MiniTabWidget, FancyBar, FancyTabBar,
  FancyTabWidget, FancyWindow and FancyDialog are gone without a same-name replacement,
  see doc/design/3.0-MIGRATION.md
- qcanpool: remove the fancydemo and the examples and manual tests of the retired widgets
- qxapp: adopt the widgets taken over from qcanpool (QxToolButton,
  QxExtensionButton, QxMenuButton, QxMenuAccessButton, QxTabBar, QxTabWidget, QxNavBar)
- ci: add a quality job (coverage report, ASan/UBSan, clang-tidy); the sanitizers
  found and fixed two pre-existing defects in qxdock
- ci: check that the installed SDK is consumable and that scripts/new-project
  produces a buildable project
- test: add an automated test suite for qxwindow
- build: add CMakePresets.json for the common configurations
  (qt6, qt6-ninja, qt5, coverage, sanitize, wasm)
- project: add scripts/new-project to scaffold a new application
- demos: give the ribbon demo a --screenshot switch that renders the window to a file and exits
- test: add a demo screenshot regression (render sanity on every run, opt-in golden
  comparison with QTCANPOOL_VISUAL_BASELINE=1, per-platform goldens)
- docs: update the migration guide for the 3.1 legacy cleanup

3.0.0
---
- qt: Qt6-first, primary support Qt 6.5 LTS / 6.8 LTS; best-effort Qt 5.15
- qt: drop Qt <= 5.14 and MSVC2017
- project: cmake is the primary build system; qmake frozen (read-only)
- project: unify C++ standard to C++17
- project: unify library naming to the qx* namespace (QxRibbon/QxWindow/QxDock/QxApp/QxCore/QxTheme)
- project: provide an installable CMake package, consumable with find_package(QtCanpool)
- project: build and publish a demo for Qt for WebAssembly (online demo)
- qcanpool: freeze the legacy ribbon (ribbonbar/ribbonpage/ribbongroup/ribbonwindow)
- qcanpool: mark the legacy API deprecated, add a migration guide
- qxribbon: the only ribbon implementation
- qxwidget: renamed and relocated to qxapp (application framework)
- qxapp: add AppShell (navigation + pages + dock area + status bar + splash + layout persistence)
- qxcore: new infrastructure library (QxSettings config, QxLogger logging)
- qxtheme: new theme engine library (palette + stylesheet, runtime switch, follow system)
- ci: add a cross-platform build matrix (Linux/Windows/macOS x Qt 5.15/Qt 6.8) and a clang-format gate
- test: expand the automated test suite (qxcore/qxtheme/qxapp/qxribbon/qxdock)
- docs: add an API reference site (Doxygen), component guides and a 2.x -> 3.0 migration guide

